            <div xml:id="d806">

                <pb facs="0864" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.0031/6–1649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the united Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-16T10:00:00+01:00">June 16, 1949—10
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:08 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2314. Foreign Office prepared discuss export controls China with Martin (Deptel
                    2010, June 11) but June 21 earliest feasible date. British representative will
                    be Morland, Counselor Economic Relations Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
